<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Bonai State</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Bonaigarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A hilly princely state on the Brahmani river in northern Odisha, ruled from Bonaigarh until 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling family claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kadamba-dynasty">Kadamba dynasty</a>, and tradition dates the state to around 1500. Its early history is poorly documented.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bonai was a rugged, forested state with a largely Adivasi population, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuyan">Bhuyan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munda-people">Munda</a> communities. It was counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chota-nagpur-plateau">Chota Nagpur</a> tributary states until 1905, when it was transferred to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orissa-tributary-states">Orissa Tributary States</a>. Its hills contain iron ore deposits.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Bonai merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> on 1 January 1948 and is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundargarh">Sundargarh</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bonai-state.jpg" alt="Bonai State" width="320" height="267"><figcaption>Image: Govern britànic de l'Índia / Government of British India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BonaiKart_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bonaigarh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Adivasi religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bonai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=bonai-state" aria-label="Bonai State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6960 1374 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bonai State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7280 1630L7364 1601M7280 1630L7364 1602M7280 1630L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7280 1630h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7280 1630h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=bonai-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
